---
title: Privacy
description: >-
  What Level Up Civics collects, why, and how it is handled.
---
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block head %}
<style>
  .privacy-body { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .privacy-body h2 {
    font-family: 'Big Shoulders Display', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700; font-size: 24px; color: var(--ink);
    margin: 48px 0 12px;
  }
  .privacy-body h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
  .privacy-body p,
  .privacy-body li {
    font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--gray);
  }
  .privacy-body ul { padding-left: 20px; margin: 12px 0; }
  .privacy-body li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .privacy-updated {
    font-size: 13px; color: var(--gray); margin-top: 48px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--soft); padding-top: 24px;
  }
</style>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}

<div class="page-hero" style="min-height: auto;">
  <div class="page-hero-content">
    <div class="page-hero-eyebrow">Privacy</div>
    <h1 class="page-hero-h1">Privacy Statement</h1>
    <p class="page-hero-sub">
      The Level Up Civics Foundation takes privacy seriously. This page explains what we collect, why, and how it is handled.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="sec sec-cream">
  <div class="privacy-body">

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>When an adult advisor registers and submits a team through the Official Team Submission form, we collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>School name, and the advisor&#39;s name and email</li>
      <li>The team&#39;s division, challenge, and optional team name</li>
      <li>Project information (Project Title and Brief Project Summary)</li>
      <li>The team&#39;s Virtual Tour video file (MP4)</li>
      <li>The advisor&#39;s confirmations that the rubric was reviewed and that required student permissions are on file</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Virtual Tour videos may contain student names, voices, images, or student-created work.</p>

    <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
    <p>We use this information to administer the Battle of the Counties competition: to identify participating schools and teams, to route entries to judges, and to coordinate County Finals and the Statewide Championship.</p>

    <h2>Who sees it</h2>
    <p>Submissions are visible to judges and admins only: Level Up Civics staff, competition judges, and the county offices of education coordinating your county's program. Nothing is posted publicly without the permissions maintained by the appropriate educational agency. We do not sell, rent, or share personal information with third parties for marketing purposes.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>Registration and submission data is retained through the end of the competition year (the current program year concludes after the January 2027 Statewide Championship). After the program year, identifying student information is deleted. Aggregate and anonymized program data may be retained for reporting purposes.</p>

    <h2>Student privacy and media releases</h2>
    <p>Level Up Civics does not collect information directly from students, and it does not collect permission forms. All team information is submitted by the school's adult advisor. Parent/guardian permissions and media releases, including permission to use each student's voice and likeness, stay on file with the school, district, or county office of education. The submitting advisor confirms that the required permissions are on file before submitting.</p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>The Official Team Submission form, including Virtual Tour uploads, is hosted by eKadence. That service has its own privacy policy.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>For questions about this privacy statement or how your information is handled, contact us at <a href="mailto:info@levelupcivicsfoundation.org">info@levelupcivicsfoundation.org</a>.</p>

    <p class="privacy-updated">Last updated: October 2026</p>
  </div>
</section>

{% endblock %}
